The gradient operator is defined by $grad f = vecrow(pdv(f, x), pdv(f, y))$, so that $dv(f, s) = vu(s) dot grad f quad forall vu(s)$. Its direction is the direction of maximum increase of $f$, its magnitude $abs(grad f)$ is the maximum rate of change, and $grad f$ is perpendicular to the contours of $f(x, y)$.
